title: Keep a refunded asset account blocked

doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    `pallet_assets::refund` removed the asset account even when it was blocked, so the holder
    could burn their balance, drop the `Blocked` status together with the entry and receive the
    asset again afterwards. Refunding a blocked account now burns the balance and returns the
    deposit or consumer reference as before, but keeps a zero-balance entry that stays blocked
    until the admin thaws it, which removes the entry. A blocked holder can therefore still free
    a consumer reference forced on them by an asset owner, but can no longer lift the block.
    `freeze` fails with `NoAccount` on such an entry.

    To back this entry with a deposit, `block` now reserves `AssetAccountDeposit` from the
    freezer when the account's holder can refund it, that is when it exists through a consumer
    reference or its own deposit, or is already such an entry. The deposit is recorded in the
    new `BlockDeposits` storage item and returned to the account that placed it when the
    account is thawed, frozen or destroyed together with the asset. Blocking an account that
    already has a block deposit takes no further deposit, and the freezer must hold enough free
    balance for it. Accounts of a sufficient asset, and accounts whose deposit someone else
    placed, cannot be refunded while blocked and take no block deposit. Accounts blocked before
    this change hold no block deposit until they are blocked again.

crates:
- name: pallet-assets
  bump: minor
